  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure slides offshore today and the resulting return \nflow will bring slightly warmer temperatures and dewpoints to \nthe region. Temperatures warm into the low to mid-50s areawide \nwith some upper 40s in the far north. Heating looks to get \nimpeded by a shortwave bringing an increase in cloud cover \nduring the afternoon, but many locations will see temperatures \nsimilar to, or slightly warmer than, yesterday. Thursday is \ngoing to be the noticeably warmer day as return flow transitions\nto southerly gradient flow as low pressure approaches from the \nnorth. Full sun should allow temperatures to mix into the 60s \narea wide with southern locations nearing 70F. The combination \nof warming dewpoints and a degree of increasing cloud cover is \ngoing to make Thursday night quite mild compared to recent \nnights with temperatures only bottoming out in the mid to upper \n40s for most of the area, and low 50s for the coastal plain.\n\nLow pressure passing to the north drags a cold front through \nbeginning Thursday night, and it looks like it is going to be \nmostly dry. There is still some uncertainty with how this plays \nout coverage wise with global ensembles still unsure if showers \nare going to make it out of the mountains, but this point may \nultimately become moot since the aforementioned showers are \ndepicted to only be good for a few hundredths of an inch anyway \n(around a tenth along the International Border). The 28.00Z NAM \nnest and RRFS are a little more excited and are showing a more \norganized band of showers approaching the area, but do also \ndepict it pretty well losing the battle to the dry air to the \nsoutheast resulting in little to nothing for the majority of the\narea.\n\nAny shower activity comes to an end pretty quickly on Friday \nsetting the stage for a dry and seasonable stretch for the \nHalloween Weekend as high pressure builds right back in. \nEnsembles are still showing a signal for a more active pattern \nto start November, but also seem to want to push it back in time\nwith every new run so if/when this comes to fruition is still \nup in the air.",
